#      added new constraint to length of copied strings in ffgcls2, based on
#      TDISP setting."
#   408694634f75367471d097c0ca30281d96d40884 (2026-11-16)
#     "In ffgcdw, reset the starting search position to the top of the
#      header each time. ..." (the two commits below build on it)
#   e78291976f330608791f795a1905a4efb7bc4754 (2026-11-18)
#     "This fixes a bug introduced with the getcols.c commit of 10/21/26 ..."
#   e744cccdb3f64d2cadc5a1429a54e6341d8b093e (2026-11-18)
#     "Minor edit to previous check-in. Added a check for int overflow."
#
# ffgcls2 (fits_read_col with TSTRING) read a variable-length string into
# a 28800-byte stack buffer using the length in its heap descriptor, without
# checking that it fits (fixed-width columns were already capped by
# ffgcprll): a crafted descriptor overflowed the stack with file contents.
# It now fails with READ_ERROR. ffgcdw (fits_get_col_display_width) also
# reports a width that covers the variable-length strings ffgcls2 returns.
#
# torchfits reaches ffgcls2 only for ASCII-table string columns (fixed
# width); it reads variable-length string columns as bytes, through its own
# descriptor checks. The variable-length fixes are carried as hardening of
# the vendored tree; torchfits output does not change, and the deviation
# below keeps it that way.
#
# This is the net diff of getcols.c from cfitsio-4.7.0 to e744ccc with one
# torchfits deviation, marked in the code: ffgcls2 still returns the whole
# field of a fixed-width string column. Upstream 113781d cuts it to the
# TDISPn width when that is narrower, which would make torchfits return
# 'abcde' for a stored 'abcdefghij' with TDISPn = 'A5'
# (tests/test_cfitsio_backports.py pins this).
#
# Drop this patch when extern/VERSIONS.txt moves to a CFITSIO release that
# contains these commits, after deciding how to keep the deviation.

